# v1.13 — the defend family under the ENDEX close rule (16cb2a6).
#
# Every defend checkpoint on disk learned under the old rule, where the root
# could declare its own DEFEND operation complete. That act is now masked
# shut: the root reports the situation and COMMAND transmits ENDEX. The
# fleet still loads (masking-only, spaces frozen) but the policies have never
# been trained against the loop they now have to close.
#
# The number to watch is `closed_on_root_report_rate` — of the operations
# COMMAND closed, how many the root's own SITREP closed early. Measured on
# fireteam_defend_v12's checkpoint under the new rule: 0.22. A policy trained
# on this loop should beat that, and success/root-death should hold at the
# v1.12 confirmed levels (fireteam 0.86 / 0.15, brique 0.97 / 0.05).
#
# defend_survivor_scale stays at 0.35, confirmed 2026-08-08. Same seeds and
# step budgets as the arms they replace, so the comparison is the close rule.
fireteam_defend_v15  --scenario fireteam_defend --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35
defend_brique_v9     --scenario defend_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35
